                                    <br/><br/><div class="instruction-big">Free Trial Period</div>
 
                                    <p>1. In the event Customer elects to use the Services on a trial basis, Customer may be billed for the contracted period customer agrees to prior to accepting trial offer. Billing may commence on the date Customer accepts this Agreement (the "Trial Period"). During the Trial Period, Customer will be limited to one keyword. The subscriber limits for the Trial Period are subject to change at any time.</p>
 
                                    <p>2. Purchase. Pricing for the Services is based upon standard subscriber level Customer chooses to purchase as indicated in the Service Order or a negotiated Service Order. The Service Order is the portion of the software that records the Customer's subscriber level, term, subscription fee, payment method and other account information. If the customer is going to publish a text that exceeds the limits of the agreed plan for the month, the customer will be billed overage charges as set forth in customer&rsquo;s pricing plan. Customer's subscriber level may be upgraded (but not downgraded) at any time during the term of their Agreement. The total number of Customer subscribers multiplied by the number of monthly messages equals the total messages sent. For example, if a Customer's subscriber list is 100 and they send seven text messages out in a month, the total messages equals 700.</p>
 
